  "scope": [
    "Persisted repository-scoped Git-revision presets: exact-email my unpushed versus pinned remote-tracking tips; recent authored work plus ancestors; descendants of pinned anchor; first-parent merges into chosen local main/default branch. No new search language or general ordering toggle.",
    "Actual graph chooser, editable day count, anchor/branch choices, save/name/delete/restart persistence, refresh/cancel, loaded-versus-selected counts, shallow/budget explanations.",
    "Long omitted runs become expandable connector rows; short gaps, working changes, stashes and selected commit remain context. Raw graph indices/identities/lane origins are preserved; reused columns have separate boundary caps. Expand/collapse, keyboard/scroll and viewport ref sizing compose with existing menus and search.",
    "Explicit older-context pages use pinned tips and no-lazy-fetch through owned background reader. Shared load_more route also uses safe pages while a view is active.",
    "Latest-only reader preserves initiating Profile and blocks replacements until accepted ForecastCompletion tickets prove actual nested remote return. Exit, park, profile/reload and drop cancel generations; existing Practice-first/fallible command routing retained."
  ],
  "safety": [
    "Commands accept immutable validated object IDs; named branches/authors never become revision/shell syntax. No automatic fetching, hooks, signing, filters, fsmonitor or optional Git writes.",
    "Bounds:30000commits/query,32MiB stdout/64KiB diagnostics and15s request runtime via accepted draft transport,120s overall job. Graph paging at most1500commits/page and100000loaded total. Up to32saved presets,80Unicode characters/name,1..3650days.",
    "Connector boundary arrays allocated only on gaps; per-row representation<=48bytes regression. View rendering remains virtualized; only projected visible raw rows contribute sizing/labels.",
    "Real Git fixtures cover four merge relations, exact metacharacter email, moved refs, refs/index preservation, canceled/invalid inputs, shallow partial clones, missing promised objects and configured helper positive control. Actual pointer choose/save/expand/collapse/all-history and profile/lifecycle/nested completion tests pass."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Linux local gates only; no native Windows/macOS or live SSH/WSL execution claimed. Existing typed accepted transport is reused, with synthetic Profile and actual-completion ownership tests.",
    "Query selection is bounded and intersects the graph currently loaded/visible under branch hide/solo. Counts distinguish global selected IDs from loaded matches; explicit context paging reads only pinned tips. Refresh is needed for moved references.",
    "Unpushed means absent from locally recorded remote-tracking tips; no claim about unobserved remote/server state. My identity matches the exact current raw author email, without alias guessing.",
    "Shallow clones stop at their local history boundary and label it. Unsupported --no-lazy-fetch/missing objects fail closed, showing loaded context and an error.",
    "Remote pool/connect wait is retained by actual-completion tickets; no total transport completion deadline is claimed.",
    "Line Dossier, Symbol Biography and Change Coupling remain pending separate implementation units after this frozen usable cut."
  ],
